 Model Context Protocol (MCP) is an open protocol that standardizes how applications provide context to LLMs."},"4":{"id":"/docs/ai/introduction-2","page_id":"/docs/ai/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/introduction","content":"Through the MCP server, an MCP client can check server health and statistics, create and manage streams, topics and partitions, send and poll messages, manage consumer groups and offsets, and administer users and personal access tokens. It connects to Iggy over TCP with its own credentials, and supports **HTTP** (the default) and **stdio** transports, with stdio suited to clients running on the same machine."},"5":{"id":"/docs/ai/introduction-3","page_id":"/docs/ai/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/introduction","content":"Access is limited in two layers. The `[permissions]` section of the MCP server's configuration can restrict it to read-only operations, and the Iggy user it connects as keeps its own permissions on the server. For production use, connect as a dedicated user with the minimum permissions it needs."},"6":{"id":"/docs/ai/introduction-4","page_id":"/docs/ai/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/introduction","content":"See **MCP Server** for how to run and configure it, the full list of tools, and client setup."},"7":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","type":"page","content":"MCP Server","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","AI"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/ai/mcp"},"8":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-0","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp","content":"Run and configure the Apache Iggy MCP server, including transport, Iggy credentials and TLS."},"9":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-1","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ai/mcp#getting-started","content":"Getting started"},"10":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-2","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ai/mcp#configuration","content":"Configuration"},"11":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-3","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ai/mcp#available-tools","content":"Available tools"},"12":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-4","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ai/mcp#server","content":"Server"},"13":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-5","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ai/mcp#operation-recovery","content":"Operation recovery"},"14":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-6","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ai/mcp#streams","content":"Streams"},"15":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-7","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ai/mcp#topics","content":"Topics"},"16":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-8","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ai/mcp#partitions--segments","content":"Partitions & Segments"},"17":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-9","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ai/mcp#messages","content":"Messages"},"18":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-10","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ai/mcp#consumer-groups","content":"Consumer Groups"},"19":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-11","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ai/mcp#consumer-offsets","content":"Consumer Offsets"},"20":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-12","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ai/mcp#users--access-tokens","content":"Users & Access Tokens"},"21":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-13","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ai/mcp#resource-options","content":"Resource options"},"22":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-14","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ai/mcp#permissions","content":"Permissions"},"23":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-15","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ai/mcp#claude-desktop-integration","content":"Claude Desktop integration"},"24":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-16","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ai/mcp#docker","content":"Docker"},"25":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-17","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ai/mcp#systemd-integration","content":"Systemd integration"},"26":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-18","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp","content":"The Model Context Protocol (MCP) is an open protocol that standardizes how applications provide context to LLMs. The Apache Iggy MCP Server is an implementation of the MCP protocol for the message streaming infrastructure. It is built using the `rmcp` crate and supports both **stdio** and **HTTP** transports."},"27":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-19","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#getting-started","content":"Start an Iggy 0.10.0 or edge broker using the getting started guide. From the matching `apache/iggy` checkout, run:"},"28":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-20","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#getting-started","content":"These are the development credentials configured in that guide. Use your broker's credentials or a PAT when connecting to an existing installation."},"29":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-21","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#getting-started","content":"The Docker image for this release is `apache/iggy-mcp:0.6.0`."},"30":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-22","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#configuration","content":"The minimal viable configuration requires at least the Iggy credentials, used to create the TCP connection to the running Iggy server that the MCP server talks to. You can choose between HTTP (the default) and STDIO transports (e.g. for the local usage with tools such as Claude Desktop choose `stdio`)."},"31":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-23","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#configuration","content":"Set `telemetry.enabled = true` to export to a running collector. For HTTP export, set `transport = \"http\"` and use complete signal URLs: `http://localhost:4318/v1/logs` for logs and `http://localhost:4318/v1/traces` for traces. The MCP server does not append those paths."},"32":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-24","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#configuration","content":"The configuration file must be in the `toml` format. By default, the server looks for `core/ai/mcp/config.toml` relative to its working directory. Set `IGGY_MCP_CONFIG_PATH` to use another path. Embedded defaults are loaded first, then the file if it exists, then environment overrides."},"33":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-25","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#configuration","content":"Each setting can also be overridden using `IGGY_MCP_<SECTION>_<KEY>`, for example `IGGY_MCP_IGGY_USERNAME` or `IGGY_MCP_HTTP_ADDRESS`. Nested settings use the same underscore convention, such as `IGGY_MCP_IGGY_TLS_ENABLED`. Set `IGGY_MCP_ENV_PATH` to load a particular dotenv file. Otherwise `.env` is searched for in the current directory and its parents. Existing environment variables take precedence over dotenv values."},"34":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-26","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#configuration","content":"Run `iggy-mcp --list-config-env-vars` to print every supported MCP configuration variable and exit before loading dotenv or configuration files or creating the Tokio runtime. The output is sorted and contains names only. If a configuration field is an indexed vector, its template uses `<N>` for indices from `0` through `255`. Whole-value vectors are listed once without a placeholder."},"35":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-27","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#configuration","content":"The `token` value can be either a literal PAT or a `file:` reference such as `token = \"file:/run/secrets/iggy_pat\"`, in which case the token is read from the given file and surrounding whitespace is removed (`~/` is expanded to the home directory). A non-empty token takes precedence over the username and password."},"36":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-28","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#available-tools","content":"The MCP server exposes these 41 tools:"},"37":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-29","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#server","content":"| Tool   | Description  |\n| ------ | ------------ |\n| `ping` | Health check |","table":"table-0"},"38":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-30","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#server","content":"| Tool        | Description                                              |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `get_stats` | Server statistics (streams, topics, partitions, OS info) |","table":"table-0"},"39":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-31","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#server","content":"| Tool     | Description         |\n| -------- | ------------------- |\n| `get_me` | Current client info |","table":"table-0"},"40":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-32","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#server","content":"| Tool         | Description                 |\n| ------------ | --------------------------- |\n| `get_client` | Get specific client details |","table":"table-0"},"41":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-33","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#server","content":"| Tool          | Description                |\n| ------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `get_clients` | List all connected clients |","table":"table-0"},"42":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-34","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#server","content":"| Tool                   | Description         |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------- |\n| `get_cluster_metadata` | Cluster information |","table":"table-0"},"43":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-35","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#server","content":"| Tool       | Description                  |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `snapshot` | Collect troubleshooting data |","table":"table-0"},"44":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-36","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#operation-recovery","content":"| Tool                | Description                                          |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `resolve_operation` | Retry a retained mutation with its original identity |","table":"table-1"},"45":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-37","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#operation-recovery","content":"| Tool                | Description                                                    |\n| ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `abandon_operation` | Release retained local state without undoing the server result |","table":"table-1"},"46":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-38","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#operation-recovery","content":"An uncertain result is not proof that the operation failed. Keep the same MCP process for retained-operation recovery. Abandoning a request does not make a fresh retry safe from duplicates."},"47":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-39","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#streams","content":"| Tool          | Description      |\n| ------------- | ---------------- |\n| `get_streams` | List all streams |","table":"table-2"},"48":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-40","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#streams","content":"| Tool         | Description        |\n| ------------ | ------------------ |\n| `get_stream` | Get stream details |","table":"table-2"},"49":{"id":"/docs/ai/mcp-41","page_id":"/docs/ai/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ai/mcp#streams","content":"| Tool            | Description         |\n| --------------- | ------------------- |\n| `create_stream` | Create