mand-discriminants","content":"| Value | Command            |\n| ----- | ------------------ |\n| 33    | `PrimaryRebalance` |","table":"table-0"},"159":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-68","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#command-discriminants","content":"| Value | Command         |\n| ----- | --------------- |\n| 34    | `SegmentDelete` |","table":"table-0"},"160":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-69","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#command-discriminants","content":"| Value | Command       |\n| ----- | ------------- |\n| 35    | `CommitReply` |","table":"table-0"},"161":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-70","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#command-discriminants","content":"| Value | Command           |\n| ----- | ----------------- |\n| 36    | `PrepareProgress` |","table":"table-0"},"162":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-71","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#command-discriminants","content":"Reserved and unused ping/pong forms do not establish a session. Reply and Eviction are client-bound and rejected on replica ingress. A replica Request uses the internal routed-request header, including its group and metadata watermark."},"163":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-72","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#consensus-and-history","content":"The metadata group orders resources, users and sessions. Every partition has its own group for messages and offsets. The `group` field identifies the target. The metadata group uses `1 << 63`, while partition groups use packed stream, topic and partition IDs."},"164":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-73","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#consensus-and-history","content":"Prepare carries an operation and its body. PrepareOk acknowledges the required replication and persistence work. Commit broadcasts the commit point and a liveness token. CommitReply proves that peers still respond. A primary that cannot reach a quorum relinquishes leadership."},"165":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-74","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#consensus-and-history","content":"StartViewChange, DoViewChange and StartView establish a new view. DoViewChange includes an untrusted-log flag so a replica without proven history cannot vote as an authoritative empty log. RequestStartView probes for the current view after recovery."},"166":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-75","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#consensus-and-history","content":"Partition incarnation fields fence an old partition history. Consumer ownership generations separately fence old group members. PrimaryRebalance moves a partition primary under metadata coordination. PrepareProgress lets a slow replica report received, held and committed progress while it catches up."},"167":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-76","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#frame-integrity","content":"Replica control frames use an XxHash3-64 frame seal widened to u128. Prepare and RepairPrepare use a prepare identity hash, and a parent identity links the history. Metadata prepare bodies have their own seal. Message batches carry their batch checksums. These unkeyed hashes detect corruption, not a malicious peer. Authentication and TLS provide separate protection."},"168":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-77","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#header-layouts","content":"Every header begins with the common 128-byte frame prefix shown in Framing. The tables below list the remaining fields in wire order. Multi-byte integers are little-endian. Reserved fields are not extension space for clients. RepairPrepare uses the PrepareHeader layout with its repair command value."},"169":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-78","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#prepareheader","content":"| Offset | Bytes | Field    |\n| ------ | ----- | -------- |\n| 128    | 16    | `client` |","table":"table-1"},"170":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-79","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#prepareheader","content":"| Offset | Bytes | Field    |\n| ------ | ----- | -------- |\n| 144    | 16    | `parent` |","table":"table-1"},"171":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-80","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#prepareheader","content":"| Offset | Bytes | Field              |\n| ------ | ----- | ------------------ |\n| 160    | 16    | `request_checksum` |","table":"table-1"},"172":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-81","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#prepareheader","content":"| Offset | Bytes | Field |\n| ------ | ----- | ----- |\n| 176    | 8     | `op`  |","table":"table-1"},"173":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-82","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#prepareheader","content":"| Offset | Bytes | Field    |\n| ------ | ----- | -------- |\n| 184    | 8     | `commit` |","table":"table-1"},"174":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-83","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#prepareheader","content":"| Offset | Bytes | Field       |\n| ------ | ----- | ----------