dles larger gaps. RequestStateTransfer obtains a manifest, then RequestStateChunk and StateChunk transfer artifacts. The receiver checks each complete artifact against its manifest length and checksum before using it. The manifest has magic `ISM1`, a u32 entry count, a u8 entry length and a trailing XxHash3-64 checksum. Entries contain kind, frontier, length and checksum."},"299":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-208","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#repair-and-state-transfer","content":"| Kind | Artifact          | Current format                                   |\n| ---- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| 0    | Metadata snapshot | MessagePack version 15, readers accept 14 and 15 |","table":"table-21"},"300":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-209","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#repair-and-state-transfer","content":"| Kind | Artifact     | Current format |\n| ---- | ------------ | -------------- |\n| 1    | Client table | `ICT5`         |","table":"table-21"},"301":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-210","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#repair-and-state-transfer","content":"| Kind | Artifact    | Current format          |\n| ---- | ----------- | ----------------------- |\n| 2    | Segment log | Canonical batch records |","table":"table-21"},"302":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-211","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#repair-and-state-transfer","content":"| Kind | Artifact                             | Current format                           |\n| ---- | ------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------- |\n| 3    | Consumer offsets and partition state | `ICO1` version 9, readers accept 8 and 9 |","table":"table-21"},"303":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-212","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#repair-and-state-transfer","content":"The offset artifact also retains partition history, retry state and producer state. These internal readability windows do not provide migration from a 0.9 data directory. Use the upgrade procedure."},"304":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-213","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#repair-and-state-transfer","content":"The header definitions and command registry define the layouts. The replica transport implements preamble admission and authentication."},"305":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/commands","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/commands","type":"page","content":"Commands","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Binary Protocol"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/binary-protocol/commands"},"306":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/commands-0","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/commands","content":"The catalog of command codes, their operation bytes, and which commands are replicated."},"307":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/commands-1","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/binary-protocol/commands#catalog","content":"Catalog"},"308":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/commands-2","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/binary-protocol/commands#payloads","content":"Payloads"},"309":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/commands-3","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/binary-protocol/commands#system","content":"System"},"310":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/commands-4","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/binary-protocol/commands#streams","content":"Streams"},"311":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/commands-5","page_id":"/