 Type | Description                                                                                                                              |\n| ------ | ---- | ------------------ | ---- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 144    | 16   | `request_checksum` | u128 | Random identity for a logical metadata or session request, retained across retries. Partition and non-replicated requests leave it zero. |","table":"table-1"},"517":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-29","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#requestheader","content":"| Offset | Size | Field       | Type | Description                                                                                      |\n| ------ | ---- | ----------- | ---- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| 160    | 8    | `timestamp` | u64  | May be zero. Direct replies can echo it, but committed prepares use a server-assigned timestamp. |","table":"table-1"},"518":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-30","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#requestheader","content":"| Offset | Size | Field     | Type | Description                                        |\n| ------ | ---- | --------- | ---- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| 168    | 8    | `request` | u64  | Request number, per client. See request numbering. |","table":"table-1"},"519":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-31","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#requestheader","content":"| Offset | Size | Field       | Type | Description                   |\n| ------ | ---- | ----------- | ---- | ----------------------------- |\n| 176    | 1    | `operation` | u8   | The `Operation` discri