ed from the request. |","table":"table-3"},"570":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-82","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"| Offset | Size | Field     | Type | Description     |\n| ------ | ---- | --------- | ---- | --------------- |\n| 144    | 16   | `context` | u128 | Server context. |","table":"table-3"},"571":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-83","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"| Offset | Size | Field    | Type | Description       |\n| ------ | ---- | -------- | ---- | ----------------- |\n| 160    | 16   | `client` | u128 | Echoed client id. |","table":"table-3"},"572":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-84","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"| Offset | Size | Field | Type | Description                                                                                                                                        |\n| ------ | ---- | ----- | ---- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 176    | 8    | `op`  | u64  | Committed log position on consensus replies. Direct replies can instead carry the session epoch or zero. This field alone does not prove a commit. |","table":"table-3"},"573":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-85","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"| Offset | Size | Field    | Type | Description                                                                                        |\n| ------ | ---- | -------- | ---- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 184    | 8    | `commit` | u64  | Commit position associated with the reply. A cached committed reply retains its original position. |","table":"table-3"},"574":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-86","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"| Offset | Size | Field       | Type | Description                                                                                         |\n| ------ | ---- | ----------- | ---- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 192    | 8    | `timestamp` | u64  | Server-assigned prepare timestamp on committed replies, or the request timestamp on direct replies. |","table":"table-3"},"575":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-87","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"| Offset | Size | Field     | Type | Description                                                                                                                   |\n| ------ | ---- | --------- | ---- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 200    | 8    | `request` | u64  | Echoed request number. Non-replicated requests can reuse a number, so it is not a unique correlation id for concurrent reads. |","table":"table-3"},"576":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-88","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"| Offset | Size | Field       | Type | Description                                                                                                                                                       |\n| ------ | ---- | ----------- | ---- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 208    | 1    | `operation` | u8   | Reply operation. Server rewrites can return `64` for CreateTopic, `65` for CreatePartitions, or `68` for DeleteSegments instead of the original client operation. |","table":"table-3"},"577":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-89","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"| Offset | Size | Field   | Type  | Description |\n| ------ | ---- | ------- | ----- | ----------- |\n| 209    | 7    | padding | bytes | Zero.       |","table":"table-3"},"578":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-90","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"| Offset | Size | Field    | Type | Description                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ------ | ---- | -------- | ---- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| 216    | 4    | `status` | u32  | `0` = no header-level failure. Nonzero = an `IggyError` code for a failure decided **before** commit (authorization denial, admission reject). A nonzero status always comes with an empty body. |","table":"table-3"},"579":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-91","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"| Offset | Size | Field            | Type | Description                                                                           |\n| ------ | ---- | ---------------- | ---- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 220    | 1    | committed result | u8   | Exactly `1` marks a final committed result. Zero and unknown values provide no proof. |","table":"table-3"},"580":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-92","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"| Offset | Size | Field    | Type  | Description |\n| ------ | ---- | -------- | ----- | ----------- |\n| 221    | 3    | reserved | bytes | Zero.       |","table":"table-3"},"581":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-93","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"| Offset | Size | Field                   | Type | Description                                                                                 |\n| ------ | ---- | ----------------------- | ---- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 224    | 8    | `partition_incarnation` | u64  | Request or served partition incarnation. Poll body context carries the full served context. |","table":"table-3"},"582":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-94","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"| Offset | Size | Field    | Type  | Description |\n| ------ | ---- | -------- | ----- | ----------- |\n| 232    | 24   | reserved | bytes | Zero.       |","table":"table-3"},"583":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-95","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"Decode order for a client:"},"584":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-96","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"Read 256 bytes, check `command`. `13` (`Eviction`) rejects the connection: map the reason and close that link. `8` (`Reply`) continues."},"585":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-97","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"Read the remaining `size - 256` body bytes."},"586":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-98","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"If `status` is nonzero, this reply reports a pre-commit rejection. It does not settle an earlier uncertain attempt. The body is empty."},"587":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-99","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"Decode the body and any result section. To settle an uncertain mutation, also require the committed-result marker and matching original request identity."},"588":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-100","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#result-section","content":"Replies for all metadata operations, including their server-internal rewrites, and for the partition-plane consumer-offset writes (`StoreConsumerOffset`, `DeleteConsumerOffset`) are **result-framed**. Non-empty Register replies use the same framing. The body starts with a result section ahead of the typed payload."},"589":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-101","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#result-section","content":"Success: `count = 0`, and the typed response payload (if any) follows the 4 count bytes."},"590":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-102","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#result-section","content":"Business or transient rejection: one entry `{ index: 0, result: error_code }` and no payload."},"591":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-103","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#result-section","content":"A nonzero header `status` has an empty body. With `status = 0`, decode the result section for the operations above: it can report either a committed outcome or a pre-commit transient rejection. Its presence alone does not prove commitment. A matching final result also needs the committed-result marker at byte 220. Replayed PAT creation cannot return the original secret and can report `PersonalAccessTokenAlreadyExists` with that proof. A successful login-register reply starts with `count = 0`, followed by the login response payload. An empty Register body is a terminal failure, not a successful login."},"592":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-104","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#result-section","content":"Replies to non-replicated commands aren't result-framed: after `status = 0` the body is the response payload directly."},"593":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-105","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#evictionheader","content":"Server to client. 256 bytes, never a body. An eviction has no per-request correlation. Close the affected link. A stale-client eviction can occur while the logical session is still live, so try binding the retained session before replacing it. A terminal bind refusal requires a new registration."},"594":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-106","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#evictionheader","content":"| Offset | Size | Field      | Type | Description                   |\n| ------ | ---- | ---------- | ---- | ----------------------------- |\n| 0      | 16   | `checksum` | u128 | Zero on client-facing frames. |","table":"table-4"},"595":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-107","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#evictionheader","content":"| Offset | Size | Field           | Type | De