nsport. HTTP supports ordinary consumers only."],[3342,"**Consumer groups**: `client.group` manages groups (including ensure-and-join in one call), and `client.message.reader` or `client.consumerGroup` reads the assigned partitions. A one-shot poll names one partition."],[3343,"**Consumer streams**: A high-level consumer supports async iteration, handler-based consumption and `toReadable()`."],[2655,"**Consumer.** A client that reads messages on its own rather than as part of a consumer group. Its position is kept separately from every other consumer's."],[3193,"**ConsumerGroupClient** - create, get, list, delete consumer groups"],[3192,"**ConsumerOffsetClient** - get, store, delete consumer offsets"],[2955,"**Consuming a topic as an async stream** (`IAsyncEnumerable`)"],[369,"**Create consumer group. Code: 602.**"],[348,"**Create partitions. Code: 402.**"],[389,"**Create personal access token. Code: 42.**"],[340,"**Create stream. Code: 202.**"],[345,"**Create topic. Code: 302.**"],[377,"**Create user. Code: 33.**"],[476,"**Create** requests resolve absent keys to server defaults and persist the effective values. Updates use explicit reset keys to restore defaults. Zero retention sentinels do not reset a value. See update semantics."],[2409,"**Custom memory pool** with 28 buckets (buffer sizes from 4 KiB to 512 MiB) for on-demand allocation, buffer reuse and sharing without copying buffer contents"],[2100,"**Custom Queries**: Use custom SQL with parameter substitution instead of simple table polling"],[1102,"**Data transformation**: Supports data transformation with the help of existing functions."],[1323,"**Decoding**: A loaded descriptor extracts present fields. Integer, boolean, and string fields become JSON values. Bytes become base64 and nested messages become metadata with base64 content. Missing fields are not filled with protobuf defaults, and float/double fields produce `unsupported_wire_type` placeholders. Without a descriptor, the default decoder returns an Any envelope's `type_url` and base64 `value`."],[2671,"**Deferred polling.** A read that waits on the server for messages or a deadline. A grouped fetch reads several partitions of one primary."],[2101,"**Delete / Mark Processed**: Optionally delete rows or flag them in a boolean column after acknowledgement"],[370,"**Delete consumer group. Code: 603.**"],[363,"**Delete consumer offset. Code: 122.**"],[349,"**Delete partitions. Code: 403.**"],[391,"**Delete personal access token. Code: 43.**"],[350,"**Delete segments. Code: 503.**"],[342,"**Delete stream. Code: 203.**"],[347,"**Delete topic. Code: 303.**"],[379,"**Delete user. Code: 34.**"],[1086,"**delete_fields** - remove existing fields from the message payload."],[333,"**Describe options. Code: 13.**"],[4033,"**Do not copy a Linux page count into `MIMALLOC_RESERVE_HUGE_OS_PAGES`.** That mimalloc option counts **1 GiB pages**. A value of `2048` requests 2 TiB, whereas `vm.nr_hugepages=2048` represents 4 GiB only when the default HugeTLB page size is 2 MiB. A 2 MiB pool does not provide a matching 1 GiB reservation."],[2732,"**Do not prepend anything** to the token. Strings like `iggypat-...` appear only in Iggy's own test code. A real token with a prefix added will fail to log in."],[2657,"**Durability.** A topic setting, `replicated` or `persisted`, that decides what must be done before a write is reported as successful. See Durability."],[1099,"**Dynamic Loading**: Supports dynamic loading of plugins, allowing integration with various data sources and sinks at runtime."],[1575,"**dynamic_route_field**: The top-level message field that specifies the Iceberg table to route data to. Ignored in static mode. See more details below."],[1574,"**dynamic_routing**: Enables dynamic routing. See more details later in this document."],[1101,"**Easy Customization**: Provides a simple interface for implementing custom connectors, making it easy to create new plugins."],[3639,"**Embedded defaults**: the `config.toml` compiled into the binary."],[4106,"**Embedded Web UI** at `/ui`, which requires `web_ui = true` in `[http]` (**off by default**) on a server built with the `iggy-web` feature (part of the default build) and the Web UI static assets. Build the assets before compiling the server. See Configuration."],[2445,"**Embedded** - compiled into the server binary (with the `iggy-web` feature and built static assets), served at the `/ui` endpoint when `http.web_ui = true`"],[1337,"**Encoding Errors**: Errors encoding a loaded message descriptor are returned to the caller. The encoder does not retry that message as Any. The decoder attempts Any after a schema decoding error."],[1322,"**Encoding**: A loaded message descriptor encodes matching JSON fields. The encoder supports booleans, strings, all protobuf integer types, and base64 strings for bytes or already-encoded nested messages. Float, double, and enum fields are unsupported by the encoder. Nested JSON objects, repeated fields, maps, and proto2 groups are not a general-purpose schema conversion path."],[3641,"**Environment variables**: any `IGGY_`-prefixed override."],[3345,"**Errors**: the package exports `ResponseError`, `DeserializeError`, `ProtocolFrameError`, and `VsrEvictionError` for precise error handling."],[716,"**Exactly one** polling strategy is required:"],[3182,"**Examples:**"],[1336,"**Fallbacks**: Missing files, compilation failures, absent schema sources, or an unmatched `message_type` can return `Ok(())` without an active message descriptor. Successful reloads into fallback mode clear the previous descriptor. Invalid protobuf syntax and malformed descriptor bytes return errors. Check the actual encoded/decoded result when validating a schema setup."],[4186,"**Federated issuers**: the opt-in `[[http.jwt.trusted_issuers]]` list accepts tokens minted by external identity providers for application-to-application flows. Each entry names an `issuer`, `audience`, and `jwks_url`. Signatures are verified against the issuer's JWKS (fetches are rate-limited), and every token from that issuer is remapped onto the configured non-root `username`. With no entries configured, the listener accepts only self-issued tokens. See Configuration for the key reference."],[1325,"**Field Mapping**: Encoder/decoder mappings use protobuf field names as keys and JSON field names as values. The encoder applies that mapping in reverse. Transform mappings rename JSON input keys directly."],[1087,"**filter_fields** - keep or drop fields based on key and value patterns."],[2571,"**First / Last** - start from the beginning or the end of the partition."],[4387,"**Fix:** check the server has started before starting the client. It logs a `server client listeners started` line that includes the address, for example `tcp=127.0.0.1:8090`. You can also check the port directly:"],[4404,"**Fix:** nothing needs fixing. The stream exists and can be used as it is. Check with `iggy stream list` before creating it if you're running a setup script more than once."],[4395,"**Fix:** run the container with `--security-opt seccomp=unconfined` and `--ulimit memlock=-1:-1`, or with a custom seccomp profile and a locked-memory limit big enough for the server. See Why these capabilities? and Linux tuning."],[4391,"**Fix:** set `IGGY_TCP_ADDRESS=0.0.0.0:8090`, and the equivalent for any other transport you expose, along with `IGGY_NODE_ADVERTISED_ADDRESS`. See the `docker run` and Compose examples in Docker & Helm."],[4398,"**Fix:** upgrade the host kernel to 5.19 or newer. Under WSL2, run `wsl --update`. Containers use the host's kernel, so it's the host that needs upgrading. See System requirements."],[1090,"**flat_buffer_convert** - convert messages between FlatBuffers and other formats."],[1104,"**Flexible configuration providers**: Support for local file-based and HTTP-based configuration providers for centralized configuration management."],[1339,"**Format Options**: Encoder `preserve_unknown_fields`, `compact_encoding`, `validate_message`, and `deterministic_encoding` are accepted but have no effect. Decoder `preserve_unknown_fields` retains unknown varints as numbers and length-delimited data as base64. Fixed-width unknown fields become placeholders. It does not retain the original wire encoding. See the Transforms page for conversion-specific limits."],[3174,"**Format:**"],[1410,"**GCS**: `gcs_service_account_key` (the service account JSON as a string, with the bucket taken from the `gs://` URI)."],[336,"**Get client. Code: 21.**"],[337,"**Get clients. Code: 22.** Empty payload."],[332,"**Get cluster metadata. Code: 12.** Empty payload."],[367,"**Get consumer group. Code: 600.**"],[368,"**Get consumer groups. Code: 601.**"],[360,"**Get consumer offset. Code: 120.**"],[335,"**Get me. Code: 20.** Empty payload."],[388,"**Get personal access tokens. Code: 41.** Empty payload."],[330,"**Get snapshot. Code: 11.**"],[329,"**Get stats. Code: 10.** Empty payload."],[338,"**Get stream. Code: 200.**"],[339,"**Get streams. Code: 201.** Empty payload."],[343,"**Get topic. Code: 300.**"],[344,"**Get topics. Code: 301.**"],[375,"**Get user. Code: 31.**"],[376,"**Get users. Code: 32.** Empty payload."],[3419,"**Getting started** - the basic example which is discussed in the getting started guide."],[3295,"**getting-started** - basic producer and consumer"],[3386,"**getting-started** - producer and consumer with optional TLS via `TcpConfig`"],[3220,"**gettingstarted** - basic blocking producer and consumer, the best starting point."],[4144,"**Global permissions** - apply to the whole server and all streams"],[3338,"**heartbeatInterval**: the client pings the server every 5 seconds by default. `0` disables heartbeats. When server heartbeat eviction is enabled, silent consumer-group members can be evicted, so keep it well below the server's heartbeat timeout."],[1096,"**High Performance**: Utilizes Rust's performance characteristics to ensure fast data ingestion and egress."],[3503,"**High-level API