ourself. The environment **takes precedence** over the flag. The credentials initialize the stored root account **only on first creation**. Changing them on a later boot does not reset its password. Supplied environment credentials are still validated on restarts."],[2983,"A batch also flushes once its accumulated payload reaches `IggyPublisherConfig.BackgroundMaxBatchBytes` (default 256 KiB, `0` disables the byte gate) - whichever of `batchSize` or the byte limit is hit first. This knob has no builder method. Set it on the config directly if needed. Await `WaitUntilAllSendsAsync` before disposal to finish queued sends. Disposal alone can discard them. Background send calls return an empty confirmation list before delivery, and failures are reported through the subscribed events."],[784,"A cached login session token (created by `iggy login`)."],[2586,"A checkpoint records a processed position with its partition history and ownership generation. A continuation carries the next read position with the same context. These prevent an old read or commit from silently applying to a recreated partition. See Multi-leader partitions and Deferred polling."],[4368,"A checkpoint records how far a consumer processed a partition. The current poll API defaults to manual commits. Rust high-level consumers also default to manual commits, and the stream builder starts with `PollingStrategy::next()`."],[2923,"A checkpoint retains the partition history and owner. A commit after a partition recreation or ownership change is refused. `polled.Continuation` continues the same partition without losing that context."],[809,"A cluster has a metadata primary and separate partition primaries. SDKs discover both. Reaching the metadata primary does not mean that the same node owns every partition request."],[4400,"A cluster replica without credentials waits for the root account to arrive through replication. Provision the same initial credentials on all replicas so any promoted node can initialize